.TH AXIOM-FIREWALL 1 "November 2026" "Axiom 0.59.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
axiom-firewall \- network and AI agent security (desktop application)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axiom-firewall
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B axiom-firewall
starts the Axiom desktop application: a per-application firewall with connection
monitoring, history, Privacy Shield DNS filtering and AI-agent awareness.
The window talks to the privileged background service
.B axiomd
over a local socket; the desktop process itself never runs as root.
.PP
The package registers
.B axiomd
as a systemd unit and installs the polkit action used to install or upgrade it.
Rules are enforced with nftables and, where available, a connect-time eBPF layer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/axiom-firewall
Desktop application and the bundled daemon publish tree.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/axiom-firewall
Launcher for the desktop application.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/axiom
Root-owned copy of the daemon image, installed by
.B axiomd --install-service
and audited on every start.
.TP
.I /var/lib/axiom
Rules, settings, history and the Privacy Shield DNS backup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR nft (8)
.PP
Documentation: https://github.com/a-51-50/Axiom
